/-- **The grid step `n`'s certificate**: its `q`-interval `[q_lo, q_hi]` covers
`[n/400, min((n+1)/400, 11/20)]`, serves the ladder lengths `K ≤ K_b` (every `K`
when `K_b = 0`, else `q_hi < ½` and `(K_b + 1)(1 - 2q_hi) ≥ 1`), and certifies every
cell of `RMF.c3Theta`, at `c3FloorTab n` and at `c3CellTab n j`. -/
theorem c3Step_spec (n : ℕ) (hn : n ≤ 220) :
    ∃ q_lo q_hi : ℝ, ∃ Kb : ℕ, (0 ≤ q_lo ∧ q_lo ≤ (n : ℝ) / 400
      ∧ min (((n : ℝ) + 1) / 400) (11 / 20) ≤ q_hi ∧ q_hi ≤ 1
      ∧ (Kb ≠ 0 → q_hi < 1 / 2 ∧ 1 ≤ Kb ∧ 1 ≤ ((Kb : ℝ) + 1) * (1 - 2 * q_hi)))
      ∧ C3IntervalCert c3Theta 24 q_lo q_hi (c3FloorTab n) Kb
      ∧ ∀ j < 24, C3CellCert q_lo q_hi (c3Theta j) (c3Theta (j + 1)) (c3CellTab n j)
        (fun K => Kb = 0 ∨ K ≤ Kb) := by
  interval_cases n
  · exact ⟨0, (1 / 100), 1, by norm_num, c3Interval_0, c3Cells_0⟩
